  ],
  "mach:judgement": "Adopt",
  "mach:judgementReason": "The most rigorous open benchmark for evaluating LLMs on health conversations to date — 5,000 multi-turn cases with 48,562 physician-written rubric criteria across 262 physicians in 60 countries. MIT licence, ships with evaluation code in openai/simple-evals. Rubric-based grading captures nuance that multiple-choice benchmarks miss, making it directly applicable to assessing clinical AI safety and accuracy. Already adopted by major model providers and research groups as a standard reference. Adopt as the primary benchmark for any team evaluating LLMs on clinical dialogue.",
  "mach:editorialReviewedAt": "2026-05-25",
